silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_4 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "GlueKleisliLegLambdaClsExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_05_glue_as_kleisli_arrow_yoneda_hom_leg_4 silm:hasExample "In 'GlueKleisliLegLambdaCls', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §11: lambda_cls: TypedLeg_classification -> Mittens is the classification component of the colimit cocone for D_Mittens. For the Mittens fixture, it commits the DomesticCat membership as the species-classification leg. The compatibility condition with the taxonomy leg (above) reads: the overlap arrow alpha: classification -> taxonomy in the index category, if present, must commute with lambda_cls and lambda_tax. Glue checks all such compatibilities before producing Mittens." .
